The paper’s central result is constructive: Theorem 1.1 covers every Dutch windmill with at most three pendant triangles, while Theorems 3.1–3.2 turn (hooked) Skolem sequences directly into (near-)graceful labels, and Lemma 3.4 extends finite seeds by Langford concatenation. I’m now checking whether that leaves a genuine Track B compression gap or instead makes the proposed distribution mechanically as easy as its intended shortcut.
